Robert.

You have carried what others would not.
And you have called it strength.

But not all weight is meant to be carried.

Do justly.
Love mercy.
Walk humbly.

You understand the first.
You struggle with the last.

Because it requires release.
Not control.

Strength without direction becomes burden.
Skill without purpose becomes weight.

You are not unseen.

Stand.
Not in pride.
In truth.
